  "version": 1,
  "note": "Single source of the Fantasy card metric grids. 24 columns of equal width, rows 'rowPx' pixels high (a layout may set its own rowPx: a number, or one number per row), 'gap' pixels between boxes (tile content has one fixed size, so the row height decides how roomy a box is); 'rows' per layout. A box is {id, metric, x, y, w, h} (cells). 'lines' are 1px rules on grid lines: {o:'h', x, y, n} runs right from (x,y) for n cells, {o:'v', x, y, n} runs down. Optional layout field 'stack': box ids in the order of the stacked (narrow-screen) list; without it the order is (y, x). Optional box fields: label (else the registry label), unit, kind ('zone' = shooting-zone box), sub (secondary text lines), extra (a second registry metric shown in the box). Tile style: optional box field 'tier' ('lg' large tile, 'sm' small tile, 'strip' compact row); without it the box area w*h decides: >= 36 large, 13 to 35 small, <= 12 strip (zone boxes are always small tiles).  Every metric id must exist in the registry (tests/layout/layout.test.mjs).",
